\f1\fs22 Detective Superintendent Hayley Lanning was a good cop in a deformed universe of bad cops. And what she knew of Lieutenant Alexander Koalemos proved he was a dolt of singular disposition. Of course, the rank of lieutenant\'97which had never existed in any Ulyssian police force prior, and which floated apart from the normal chain of command\'97should have alerted anyone with the curiosity of bathroom mold (which admittedly excluded every other detective in the police force) as to Koalemos\'92s fitness for service. But, to Hayley\'92s chagrin, his career remained largely unexamined.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Well, tax my trust funds, she was examining them now.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Whispers circulated that his assignments hailed directly from the Commissioner\'92s office, and Koalemos was being deliberately dispatched to seal cases the powers-that-be would rather not see scrutinised. But Hayley was examining them, over a fevered weekend since she\'92d learned Koalemos was taking over the Nightclub Vampire case. Her case! Given the cavalier history of his case files\'97which from the start had been incoherent and often contained copyright-infringing reprints of Larson cartoons as \'91evidence\'92 (Koalemos apparently favoured the ones with cows)\'97had deteriorated to dismissive one-liners. For example, this latest report regarding one Travis Teh, which demanded not a single flick of the scroll-bar on her display; it merely stated, 
\fs18 CASE CLOSED: SUICIDE
\fs20 .\
